<title>GERMANY: German metal union/employers delay news conference.</title>
<headline>German metal union/employers delay news conference.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The news conference scheduled for 1500 GMT to follow the emergency meeting between metals union IG Metall and the employers' union Gesamtmetall over cuts and sick pay, has been delayed.</p>
<p>Sources close to the negotiations said they did not expect the meeting &quot;to go on all night&quot;, but no immediate announcement was expected.</p>
<p>German unions have been angered by a new law reducing sick pay to 80 percent from 100 percent, aimed at cutting labour costs. The unions say such benefits have been hard won in negotiation and cannot be simply abolished overnight.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
